TY  - JOUR
ID  - R12384
TI  - Toxicity and biodegradation of two different hydrothermal liquefaction process waters for anaerobic digestion and the effect of microaeration
AU  - Zhou, Mei
AU  - Usack, Joseph G.
AU  - Smith, Aidan Mark
AU  - Angenent, Largus T.
PY  - 2025
JO  - Chemical Engineering Journal
VL  - 520
DO  - 10.1016/j.cej.2025.165540
AB  - Hydrothermal liquefaction (HTL) can convert a considerable portion of the carbon in complex feedstocks into renewable bio-oil, but it also generates an aqueous phase ( i.e. , HTL process water) that retains >30% of the carbon from the HTL feedstock. Feeding HTL process water to anaerobic digestion (AD) is a promising approach for maximizing resource recovery, enabling the conversion of the retained carbon into biogas. However, various toxic and poorly biodegradable compounds in the HTL process water make its treatment with AD challenging. Presently, the underlying mechanisms remain unclear. We investigated the impact of HTL process water from two different feedstocks – a food-waste proxy ( i.e. , dog food, rich in proteins) and wheat straw (rich in lignocellulose) – on the different trophic groups in the food web of AD. We found that methanogens, rather than acidogens, were more severely inhibited by HTL process water. Comparative toxicity and biodegradability analyses showed that wheat-straw process water had a higher methane potential of 189 ± 1.52 mL CH 4 /g COD than that of food-waste process water with a potential of 130 ± 0.13 mL CH 4 /g COD, regardless of its higher toxicity to acetoclastic methanogens. The use of microaeration-acclimated biomass improved the methane yields of food-waste process water by 38% compared to anaerobic biomass, even without oxygen addition. However, the use of microaeration-acclimated biomass or microaeration was ineffective for wheat-straw process water. These findings highlight the importance of feedstock-specific strategies to optimize AD for biogas production from HTL process water.
SP  - 165540
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2025.165540
KW  - 1 直接向 AD 反应器或内部循环系统供氧
